Direct3D 10: say which resource was refused, in the driver's own log

When the renderer has no format for a resource the driver answers "out of memory", as the
interface wants, and said why only in debug builds. Now it writes a line to the driver's log
(RippleLog, windows/mesa/overlay-virgl: the debugger's output, and a file when RIPPLE_UMD_LOG
is set). The test after creating the resource looked at the wrong pointer and never fired; it
now tests the resource.

35:#include "Format.h"
diff -ru a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/meson.build b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/meson.build
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/meson.build
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
     'Query.cpp',
     'Rasterizer.cpp',
     'Resource.cpp',
+    'RippleLog.cpp',
     'Shader.cpp',
     'ShaderDump.cpp',
     'ShaderParse.c',
diff -ru a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 
 #include "Resource.h"
 #include "Format.h"
+#include "RippleLog.h"
 #include "State.h"
 #include "Query.h"
 
@@ -329,16 +330,21 @@
